#: woocommerce/woocommerce.php:408
msgid "How the product transients are purged"
msgstr ""

#: woocommerce/woocommerce.php:409
msgid "By default, we purge the product transients immediately after a product is edited, this allows you to see the changes applied in the front end instantly. But if your site receives a lot of visitors and you do many product edits, purging transients often can cause performance degradation, so you might want to delay the purge to a more convenient time"
